WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.635
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.236
You're here.
You made it.

00:00:04.236 --> 00:00:07.106
Thank you for watching at home.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:11.143
Well, guys, the Tokyo Olympics
have officially come to an end.

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:13.312
Yeah, that's right.
Now if you want to witness

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:15.081
physical excellence,
you'll have to watch

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.150
a flight attendant duct-tape
a drunk guy to his seat.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.486
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.486 --> 00:00:23.056
Seriously, give that flight
attendant a medal, I think.

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:24.390
Come on.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.827
That guy...

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.762
But it was a magical two weeks.

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:32.098
Night after night,
Americans gathered around the TV

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:34.400
to see the events where we
already saw who won on Twitter.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.268
[ Laughter ]
It was just an amazing --

00:00:36.268 --> 00:00:38.771
But this was exciting.
After an incredible last day,

00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:43.209
Team USA topped the final
medal count with 113 medals!

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.677
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.045
That's right.

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:49.582
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.650
That's right -- 113 medals.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.385
Meanwhile, all the country
wants to talk about

00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:55.388
is how often celebrities bathe.

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.123
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.524
That's right.
The Olympics are over,

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:01.527
but if you're still craving
exciting, pulse-pounding sports,

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:04.097
ESPN's got you covered.
Check it out.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.903
There you go.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:13.572
All day long.
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:13.572 --> 00:01:15.208
Let's get to some news.
On Friday,

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.443
the White House announced
that half of all Americans

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:19.312
are now fully vaccinated.

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:24.717
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.519
And this is cool.
To get those numbers up,

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.188
in the fall,
Pfizer just announced

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:29.589
a new pumpkin-spice vaccine.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:32.391
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.391 --> 00:01:33.593
That's right.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:37.129
50% of the country
is fully vaccinated.

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:39.365
Is it just me, or does it
feel like a group project

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:41.100
where half the team
does all the work?

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:44.603
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:44.603 --> 00:01:47.073
"What are you doing?"

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:49.375
Speaking of the vaccine,
United Airlines announced

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.110
that they're requiring
all of their employees

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.978
to get vaccinated.

00:01:52.978 --> 00:01:54.347
But this is annoying.

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:57.417
They're now charging every
passenger a $9 common-sense fee.

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:59.118
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:00.986
Meanwhile, Spirit Airlines
isn't requiring vaccines.

00:02:00.986 --> 00:02:02.221
They were just like,

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:03.856
"We're just gonna fly
with the windows down."

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:08.361
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.361 --> 00:02:10.963
Some more business news.
I saw that KFC is opening

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:13.032
a hotel in London
that will feature

00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:17.036
a "Press for Chicken" button
in every room.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:20.073
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:21.940
-Finally!
-If you're wondering who stays

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:24.910
at the KFC hotel,
just picture the exact opposite

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:26.746
of the Olympic Village.
That's who's --

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.013
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.013 --> 00:02:29.616
And did you see this?
In Oklahoma,

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:32.985
a truck carrying
more than 27,000 pounds

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:35.254
of women's
spray deodorant exploded.

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:36.689
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:39.358
It was the first truck explosion
ever described as "Confident,

00:02:39.358 --> 00:02:41.360
strong, and ready
to take on the day."

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:44.063
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:46.799
And, finally, I saw that
London's Tower Bridge

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:48.901
was stuck open today,

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.602
causing traffic
to a grind to a halt.

00:02:50.602 --> 00:02:53.005
You know the Queen was
at home, going, "I'm starving.

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:54.507
Where the F
is my Uber Eats guy?"

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.275
[ Laughter and applause ]
We have a great show, everybody.

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:58.278
Give it up for The Roots!

00:02:58.278 --> 00:02:59.778
-♪ My mind designed
a finer rhyme ♪

00:02:59.778 --> 00:03:01.247
♪ And right on time,
I'mma step beyond ♪

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:02.681
♪ And not behind a line ♪

00:03:02.681 --> 00:03:04.116
♪ Celebrate dawn for the rise ♪

00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:05.418
[ Rapping indistinctly ]

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.686
♪ As a warning sign ♪

00:03:06.686 --> 00:03:08.587
♪ Antonyms, words on
synonyms, homonyms ♪

00:03:08.587 --> 00:03:10.656
♪ Cinnamon spelled like M&amp;M's ♪

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:12.191
♪ Hey, yeah ♪

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:14.126
♪ To retain them again ♪

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:16.228
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.228 --> 00:03:17.897
-It is Monday, everybody!

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.965
We got a brand-new show tonight.

00:03:19.965 --> 00:03:21.968
Billie Eilish is here!

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:25.972
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:27.540
We have actually a giant week.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.775
A giant week of shows this whole
week on "The Tonight Show."

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:32.044
Tomorrow night,
Barbra Streisand will be here.

00:03:32.044 --> 00:03:34.380
-Ooh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.549
-Billy Crystal will be here.
-Hey!

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:37.783
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.783 --> 00:03:40.453
-Kit Harington,
Duran Duran will be here.

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:41.521
-Oh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.822
-All-new "Tonight Shows"
the whole week.

00:03:43.822 --> 00:03:46.859
We also have our author
of the Fallon Summer Reads.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:48.294
"Our author."
-"Our author."

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:49.962
-Yeah.
It's everyone's.

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:53.132
America's author.
Jean Hanff Korelitz

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:54.867
will be on the show Wednesday
to talk about her --

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:58.037
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.672
"The Plot" is the book,

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:00.806
and I just finished it
this morning.

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:03.609
-Did you really?
Nuts.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:04.844
-It's unbelievable.

00:04:04.844 --> 00:04:08.181
Twists, turns,
turns upon twists.

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:10.349
And then twists one more time.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:12.718
It's like Chubby Checker.
-Does it twist again?

00:04:12.718 --> 00:04:14.387
-Twist against
like we did last summer,

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:16.389
that song, the follow-up hit
to "The Twist."

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:17.957
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:19.758
He's like, "I got it."
-What is it?

00:04:19.758 --> 00:04:21.427
What's the new hit?

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.062
-How many years has it been
since "The Twist"?

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.598
-Like two?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:26.999
But you got another song in you.
I know you do.

00:04:26.999 --> 00:04:30.402
-Yep. Well, "The Twist"
went like this, right?

00:04:30.402 --> 00:04:32.772
♪ Come on, baby ♪

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.607
♪ Let's do the twist ♪

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:36.975
Check it out.
That's -- That's the old me.

00:04:36.975 --> 00:04:38.845
-That's the old you.
-That's the old me.

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:40.179
I don't even remember that dude.

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:42.315
-Yeah, that guy's gone,
'cause this is the new

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:44.784
Chublin P. Checker.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:46.052
Lay it on them.
Lay that song on them.

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:47.720
-Now, people think they call
me chubby because --

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.756
-Right, because of Fats Domino.
-Yeah.

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:51.991
But no I'm --
No, my real name is Chublin.

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:54.927
-Chublin P. Checker.
-Chublin P. Checkers.

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:56.429
Checker.
Sorry. Not Checkers.

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:58.498
That's ridiculous.
So Chubby Checker...

00:04:58.498 --> 00:04:59.699
-Yes.
-...who lost weight

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:01.066
doing "The Twist," by the way.
-Right.

00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:03.936
-It was like a diet fad.
-It's an aerobic.

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:05.570
-He was hitting all the bases.
-Right.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:06.805
-So I got you a song.

00:05:06.805 --> 00:05:07.940
"You want a hit song?
You got it.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.808
Do you want to lose weight?
You got it.

00:05:09.808 --> 00:05:11.411
Let's do 'The Twist.'"

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:13.780
Everybody does The Twist,
and now he just goes by,

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:17.083
you know, uh, Jared Checker.

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:19.218
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:21.320
So he goes --
Yeah, so he's Jared Checker.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:22.688
He's like,
"I lost all this weight."

00:05:22.688 --> 00:05:25.357
And then you go,
"No. Keep 'Chubby.'" Right?

00:05:25.357 --> 00:05:27.092
But how do you follow it up
with a second --

00:05:27.092 --> 00:05:28.928
-What could possibly be --

00:05:28.928 --> 00:05:31.297
-Let's not Twist
and gain it back.

00:05:31.297 --> 00:05:34.333
-Right.
-So Chubby goes, "I got it."

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:36.769
-What's your song?
I can't wait to the hear it.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:38.804
♪ Let's Twist again ♪

00:05:38.804 --> 00:05:41.006
♪ Like we did last summer ♪

00:05:41.006 --> 00:05:42.908
Yeah.
He does "Let's Twist Again."

00:05:42.908 --> 00:05:45.411
That was his follow-up hit.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:48.347
And then --
Did he have any other hits?

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:51.284
-Yes, "Still Twisting."
-"Still Twisting," yeah.

00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:52.885
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:54.553
-He did not. Did he?
-Yeah, he did.

00:05:54.553 --> 00:05:56.121
-He did.
-"Still Twisting."

00:05:56.121 --> 00:05:57.322
-"Still Twisting"?
No, you're making that up.

00:05:57.322 --> 00:05:58.657
-I don't even know how --

00:05:58.657 --> 00:06:00.660
I know "Still Twisting's" a
song, but how does it go?

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.528
-It goes...

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.897
♪ Still Twisting ♪

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:08.166
♪ Still Twisting ♪
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.166 --> 00:06:12.805
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:14.407
"Still Twisting"
would have been a giant hit.

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:16.742
-Yeah, huge.
-But didn't he --

00:06:16.742 --> 00:06:18.043
He came back out
with The Fat Boys, didn't he?

00:06:18.043 --> 00:06:20.679
Chubby Checker?
-Yes, in '87.

00:06:20.679 --> 00:06:21.947
-Yeah.
-Wow.

00:06:21.947 --> 00:06:24.116
And then was it --
-"The Twist."

00:06:24.116 --> 00:06:25.984
-Yeah.
-"Twist in '87."

00:06:25.984 --> 00:06:28.086
-Don't mess with the original
if the original's working.

00:06:28.086 --> 00:06:29.755
-Twisting it up.
The cruller.

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:31.591
-Yeah. You know, I like
classical music, right?

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:33.225
-Oh, you love it.
-You know what I say?

00:06:33.225 --> 00:06:34.560
-What do you say?

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:35.694
If it ain't baroque,
don't fix it?

00:06:35.694 --> 00:06:39.364
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.364 --> 00:06:41.200
But what a show we have
for you tonight, everybody.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.635
She has the number-one album
in the country,

00:06:43.635 --> 00:06:45.337
"Happier Than Ever."

00:06:45.337 --> 00:06:47.907
Billie Eilish is here!
We're gonna talk to Billie!

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:50.109
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:52.211
And then, she's performing
the title track

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:53.946
"Happier Than Ever"
later in the show.

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:56.348
Also, from the new film
"Stillwater,"

00:06:56.348 --> 00:07:00.353
Abigail Breslin is here!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:00.353 --> 00:07:02.622
Abigail Breslin!

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:04.523
We love her.

00:07:04.523 --> 00:07:06.625
Guys, before we go on,
I'd like to take a moment

00:07:06.625 --> 00:07:08.861
to thank some of our sponsors
for tonight's show.

00:07:08.861 --> 00:07:11.664
They don't always fit in the
commercial breaks, apparently.

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:13.900
So we want to make sure --
[ Light laughter ]

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:15.834
-Right.
-According to the cue cards.

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:17.403
Yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:17.403 --> 00:07:19.438
We want to make sure that we
mention all of the --

00:07:19.438 --> 00:07:20.639
-Sure.
-So now it's time

00:07:20.639 --> 00:07:22.542
for a thing called
"Tonight Show Sponsors."

00:07:22.542 --> 00:07:23.743
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:26.546
-♪ Tonight Show Sponsors ♪

00:07:26.546 --> 00:07:30.482
♪ Tonight Show Sponsors ♪

00:07:30.482 --> 00:07:33.218
-Now. these are sponsors that --
-Didn't make it.

00:07:33.218 --> 00:07:34.586
-To the commercial breaks.
-Right.

00:07:34.586 --> 00:07:36.088
-So we're gonna help out.
-You're gonna say them now.

00:07:36.088 --> 00:07:37.289
You're gonna
say their names now.

00:07:37.289 --> 00:07:40.259
-That's correct. Yeah.
Here's the first one.

00:07:40.259 --> 00:07:42.527
Tide -- We'll get blood
out of that shirt,

00:07:42.527 --> 00:07:44.096
and we won't ask any questions.

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:47.933
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:47.933 --> 00:07:50.102
Tombstone --
Ever wanted to destroy

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:52.237
the roof of your mouth
on something mediocre?

00:07:52.237 --> 00:07:54.140
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.808
-Wow!

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:58.677
-Target -- Somehow you just
spent 140 bucks here.

00:07:58.677 --> 00:08:02.815
We don't know how.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:02.815 --> 00:08:05.984
Fox News -- We're basically a
Facebook thread you can watch.

00:08:05.984 --> 00:08:09.788
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:09.788 --> 00:08:12.324
Oreo -- Still putting out
weird, new flavors

00:08:12.324 --> 00:08:14.426
just to remind you
the regular ones are better.

00:08:14.426 --> 00:08:17.830
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:20.166
Pizza Hut --
We're why that one bank in town

00:08:20.166 --> 00:08:21.299
looks like a Pizza Hut.

00:08:21.299 --> 00:08:25.337
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:25.337 --> 00:08:27.840
[ Laughter continues ]

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.142
Good &amp; Plenty --
There are plenty,

00:08:30.142 --> 00:08:32.244
but if you don't like licorice,
they're not good.

00:08:32.244 --> 00:08:35.147
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:37.415
Tempur-Pedic --
Want to sleep in a baby pool

00:08:37.415 --> 00:08:38.817
full of kinetic sand?

00:08:38.817 --> 00:08:41.220
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.588
Tums --
Because you're 30.

00:08:43.588 --> 00:08:45.057
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:49.027
And finally, Red Roof Inn --
Think your mattress is stained?

00:08:49.027 --> 00:08:51.096
You should have seen it
before we flipped it.

00:08:51.096 --> 00:08:53.065
That's all we have
for "Tonight Show Sponsors."

